cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  This repository is currently a pre-release research substrate. If you use it,
  cite the repository using this metadata and the exact commit or release you used.
title: "Australian For AIs: A Cultural-Pragmatics Benchmark for Ethical Language Understanding"
abstract: >-
  Australian For AIs is a cultural-pragmatics research project and benchmark
  for evaluating how artificial intelligence systems understand Australian English,
  particularly humour, irony, understatement, profanity, affectionate insults,
  social context, discourse markers, ambiguity, and intended meaning.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/QSOLKCB/AUSTRALIAN-FOR-AIS"
keywords:
  - natural language processing
  - pragmatics
  - Australian English
  - cultural bias
  - AI ethics
  - benchmark
  - sociolinguistics
  - humour
  - intent recognition
  - sentiment analysis
authors:
  - name: "Australian For AIs Contributors"
